WEBVTT

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:06.339
Hey, listen up.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.339
We want to thank everyone for coming out and support the band and out.

00:00:10.339 --> 00:00:13.339
They're really excited to be here.

00:00:13.339 --> 00:00:16.339
Thank you to talk about a concert.

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:20.339
All right, the band will be on real soon, so sit tight.

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:22.339
You ready for a great show?

00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:31.000
So, uh, we used to come to places like this together.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.950
I can't believe it's all blank.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.649
It'll come back.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:47.140
How about I reintroduce you to your favorite, Bevy?

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.140
Okay.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.140
I'll be right back.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:01:01.340
Back.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.780
Coming through.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.439
Hey, the promoter needs some gum and I'm fresh out.

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:10.439
You got me?

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:12.439
Look around, Einstein.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.439
We're in a gum factory.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:15.439
Right.

00:01:15.439 --> 00:05:22.259
I didn't forget how to use up all the hot water.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.300
But I understand that she still hasn't managed to recover her memory.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:37.160
She still thinks she's from Minnesota.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.160
I think the more she looks into her past, she'll realize it's all a lie.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:47.579
Do you think if she was taken to the fortress?

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:50.579
to the fortress might speed up the process.

00:05:50.579 --> 00:05:52.579
Last time I went to Giral for advice,

00:05:52.579 --> 00:05:54.579
he kept me prisoner in the fortress.

00:05:54.579 --> 00:05:57.579
I think it's time to tell the truth.

00:05:57.579 --> 00:06:01.089
She won't believe you.

00:06:01.089 --> 00:06:03.089
Clark, we have to protect her.

00:06:03.089 --> 00:06:04.089
I agree.

00:06:04.089 --> 00:06:13.600
Especially when she's been visiting with Lex.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.600
As much as I hate to admit it, it makes sense.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.600
He found her. She trusts him.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:24.600
Her bracelet.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.600
That connects her to Krypton.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.600
Yes.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.600
I thought it had gone missing.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.779
It has, but there's got to be some way to find it.

00:06:35.779 --> 00:06:38.779
In the meantime, I suggest you keep a sharp eye

00:06:38.779 --> 00:06:44.629
on Lex's latest endeavor.

00:06:44.629 --> 00:06:45.629
Pete Ross.

00:06:45.629 --> 00:06:47.629
What a surprise.

00:06:47.629 --> 00:06:49.629
Oh my God, Pete.

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:50.629
Hey.

00:06:50.629 --> 00:06:54.519
Pete, it's good to see you.

00:06:54.519 --> 00:06:56.519
What are you doing here?

00:06:56.519 --> 00:07:04.180
More importantly, what's he doing here?

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:07.589
I guess more's changed around here than I thought?

00:07:07.589 --> 00:07:08.589
It's a long story.

00:07:08.589 --> 00:07:43.230
I take you the fresh farm air as

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.230
as invigorating as it's cracked up to be?

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:51.339
I spend every day wandering around that place,

00:07:51.339 --> 00:07:53.339
trying to find something that will jog my memory.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:57.220
Did anything stand out?

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.220
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.860
Actually, yeah.

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.459
Everything.

00:08:05.459 --> 00:08:07.459
I don't feel connected to it at all.

00:08:07.459 --> 00:08:11.089
But thanks for finding what you did.

00:08:11.089 --> 00:08:14.089
I know it matches with the girl formerly known as Kara Kent,

00:08:14.089 --> 00:08:18.089
but the girl in that folder isn't me.

00:08:18.089 --> 00:08:25.459
How well do you know, Clark?

00:08:25.459 --> 00:08:26.459
Do you trust him?

00:08:26.459 --> 00:08:30.439
I wish I could say yes.

00:08:30.439 --> 00:08:38.759
I'm starting to wonder if he's hiding something from me.

00:08:38.759 --> 00:08:42.759
Doesn't it seem weird that I don't have any medical or dental records?

00:08:42.759 --> 00:08:44.759
Who doesn't get sick?

00:08:44.759 --> 00:08:47.759
Clark can be evasive.

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:50.759
Why would he lie to me?

00:08:50.759 --> 00:08:53.759
I mean, what in my past would be so horrible he wouldn't want me to know about it?

00:08:53.759 --> 00:08:56.759
Kara, I promise you.

00:08:56.759 --> 00:09:04.090
I will do everything in my power to help you get your memory back.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:07.090
Now, I don't suppose Clark has mentioned anything about your missing bracelet.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:09.090
No.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:18.580
And I guess I should tell you.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.580
The design on your bracelet is a symbol.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.580
A symbol that matches others that have appeared around Smallville.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:30.779
These were first seen as paintings in the Kauachi caves.

00:09:30.779 --> 00:09:33.779
They've appeared much more recently.

00:09:33.779 --> 00:09:38.799
Burned into the Kent Barn.

00:09:38.799 --> 00:09:40.799
Whatever Clark's hiding from you.

00:09:40.799 --> 00:09:43.799
I think it has something to do with these symbols.

00:09:43.799 --> 00:10:03.190
The bracelet could be the clue to uncovering your true identity.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.190
I'll see you this afternoon.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.190
You sure you don't want me to go with you?

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.190
No, it's okay, Ben.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:30.610
I'll help me unload the post.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.610
So the secret of the century is not so secret anymore.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:37.610
Lionel, Chloe, and Lana all know the truth about your extraterrestrial crash landing?

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.610
It all just kind of happened.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:45.620
Well, the truth is, with all the danger I put you in knowing my secret.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.620
I actually didn't want to tell anybody else, but...

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.620
But let me guess.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.620
You couldn't stop trying to save the world and you got caught.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:11:03.649
Let's go.

00:11:03.649 --> 00:11:05.649
Wonder what your dad would think about a Luther hanging out in his car.

00:11:05.649 --> 00:11:08.179
Catch you.

00:11:08.179 --> 00:11:09.179
Well...

00:11:09.179 --> 00:11:11.179
Two one.

00:11:11.179 --> 00:11:16.899
My dad's been gone.

00:11:16.899 --> 00:11:18.899
My dad's done a lot for me and my mom.

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:20.899
Oh.

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:23.899
Sure he has. I mean, it's done a lot for my family, too.

00:11:23.899 --> 00:11:27.899
Took our factory, caused my parents divorce.

00:11:27.899 --> 00:11:29.899
The guy's a real saint.

00:11:29.899 --> 00:11:35.899
That's the way it used to be.

00:11:35.899 --> 00:11:37.899
You can't really expect you to understand.

00:11:37.899 --> 00:11:40.899
I mean, you have been gone for over three years.

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:42.899
What have you been doing?

00:11:42.899 --> 00:11:45.690
We don't all end our dream career like that.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:47.690
Our dream career like Chloe.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.690
Kind of been doing the roadie gig.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.690
Pays the bills.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.690
Can't at least return one of my calls.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:58.929
I think it's easy saying goodbye to your best, friend.

00:11:58.929 --> 00:12:03.929
I couldn't risk anyone using me to get to the truth about your secret.

00:12:03.929 --> 00:12:06.929
I figured it was better just leaving it all in the past.

00:12:06.929 --> 00:12:11.899
I didn't ask you to do that, Pete.

00:12:11.899 --> 00:12:12.899
I know.

00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:18.730
But doesn't change the fact that I've been looking over my shoulder ever since.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.730
I mean, I had to leave my life behind because of you, Clark.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:24.419
And if you,

00:12:24.419 --> 00:12:31.820
To be honest, it was better than living in your shadow.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.820
I didn't know.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.820
Luckily, everything's changed.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:46.500
I finally brought my game up to your level, Clark.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.500
What happened to you?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.500
It doesn't matter.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:52.500
The other night, I saved this girl, and I finally got a taste

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.500
of what it felt like to be you.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:13:00.980
To be a hero.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.980
Whatever it is, we need to find a way to reverse it.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:10.240
You should have known you couldn't be happy for me.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.240
I want you to be careful.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.240
And what?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.240
How I'd like you.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.240
This isn't you.

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.240
It's the kryptonite.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.240
You know what it does? It warps your reality.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.240
The only thing warped is how many more people's lives

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:24.240
you're going to ruin by keeping your powers a secret.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.240
I'm not going to make anyone live with that burden like you did.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.240
Things change, Clark.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.240
Time to share the glory, and if you try to stop me,

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:36.240
my secret isn't going to be the only one in danger of being exposed.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:57.580
Well, who should I blame for my server problems?

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:00.580
I've been locked out of my files.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:01.580
Yes.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.580
Thank you.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.580
Open my email yet?

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:09.580
Sorry, Jimmy. I've been in IT hell all morning.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.580
Some network issues got me surfing in the slow lane.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.580
Okay, here.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:18.740
It's pretty cool, huh?

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:26.220
Oh my God.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:30.220
I know, right? This guy's elastic limbs are going to slingshot his story straight to the front page.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.220
Jimmy, this guy is Pete Ross.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.220
He was like my best friend in high school, like, back before Clark.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:40.620
You, um, ditched him for Clark?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.639
No.

00:14:43.639 --> 00:14:45.840
I mean, we were all friends.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.039
We were all best friends.

00:14:47.639 --> 00:14:50.240
Well, he is going to be an overnight superstar.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:51.500
I just got off the phone.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:57.379
He's the first meteor biologically enhanced individual.

00:15:00.759 --> 00:15:02.600
Who's willing to be interviewed about his powers?

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.399
I just need to flesh the saddle home.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:07.740
Interviewed. Are you serious?

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:08.399
Yeah.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.600
Imagine what a guy like Pete could do

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.100
for the public perception of the meteor enhanced.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:12.720
He's smart.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:13.759
He's funny.

00:15:14.519 --> 00:15:16.539
The guy's story's beyond amazing.

00:15:16.639 --> 00:15:17.240
It's great.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:20.529
Okay, so he's a war.

00:15:20.549 --> 00:15:25.769
personal ad, but Jimmy, as much as I appreciate your socially conscious attitude adjustment,

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.529
the press would turn Pete into a circus free.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:29.649
It's just an interview.

00:15:36.899 --> 00:15:37.820
You know what, maybe you're right.

00:15:39.539 --> 00:15:44.200
Do you mind if I, um, add a little purple prose just to smooth out the rough edges?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.940
Please sprinkle some of your Hemingway dust.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.039
Look, I'm off the Stride Factory.

00:15:48.039 --> 00:15:50.960
I'm going to interview a few of Elastic Man's comrades before they start in the next gig.

00:15:52.399 --> 00:15:52.980
Thank you.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.299
Thank you so much.

00:16:03.559 --> 00:16:04.480
Hey, Clark.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:07.879
We've got a problem, and it appears to be growing.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:44.500
Chloe, glad to see someone's taking advantage of my open-door policy.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:48.740
The IT department told me you've been monitoring everything that happens on the Daily Planet computers?

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.450
Unauthorized surveillance is totally unethical.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.330
Pretty big words from a cub reporter.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:57.750
Shouldn't you be using them in the right stories?

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:02.629
Good idea. I think office espionage has a nice ring to it.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:08.630
Look, I'm new here, but I thought Lois had first stab at conspiracy theory.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:12.490
You hacked into my computer and copied my files, Lex.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:13.849
I have rights.

00:17:14.009 --> 00:17:15.869
No, you don't have rights.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:18.150
You have responsibilities.

00:17:19.269 --> 00:17:21.990
Owning the daily plan, it means everything within these walls.

00:17:22.289 --> 00:17:24.869
And if you have a problem with the way I run this paper, Ms. Sullivan,

00:17:25.329 --> 00:17:28.589
you're free to find out if the Inquisitor offers the more considerate environment.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:31.509
You're excused.

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.759
So, what time's a concert tonight?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:51.680
8 o'clock.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:52.579
Thanks, bro.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:53.819
Keep living.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.700
Hey, C.K.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.019
Care to tell you about Pete's stretch save last night?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.319
Snapped his arms out like silly flight right in front of him.

00:18:01.359 --> 00:18:03.000
Maybe you didn't see what you thought you saw, Jimmy.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.859
What, you don't want to think that one of your best friends could be a meteor free?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.960
Look, I just hate to think that you have something against a meteor and ass.

00:18:11.019 --> 00:18:11.480
That's not it.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.539
I just don't want to see anything happen to Pete, that's all.

00:18:14.099 --> 00:18:14.559
Like what?

00:18:14.619 --> 00:18:15.440
Get the credit he deserves?

00:18:16.339 --> 00:18:17.359
Pete Ross is a hero.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.380
He saved Kare's life and having the courage to reveal that to the rest of the world.

00:18:21.019 --> 00:18:21.819
That's a big deal.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.440
I'm not sure that.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.119
The rest of the world is going to see it that way.

00:18:26.619 --> 00:18:29.420
Why? The world needs a hero now more than ever, Clark.

00:18:34.319 --> 00:18:36.559
Maybe meteor freaks can walk among us without being afraid.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.240
Wouldn't you want that if one was your friend?

00:19:22.769 --> 00:19:24.990
I always knew the torch would light the way to the big leagues.

00:19:25.549 --> 00:19:28.609
Pete, hey, it's so good to see you.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:31.690
Don't be too impressed, though.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:35.029
I just went from being a big fish in a small pond to a minnow in the Atlantic.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:40.190
Well, I, for one, I've read all your stories, and as much as some things change,

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.569
some things always remain the same.

00:19:41.589 --> 00:19:43.990
I couldn't agree more.

00:19:44.289 --> 00:19:48.890
I'm actually in the process of mopping up Lex Luthor's daily carnage as we speak.

00:19:50.029 --> 00:19:51.029
Now, there's the name I don't miss?

00:19:51.829 --> 00:19:54.930
He's playing Big Brother on all of the computers at the Daily Planet.

00:19:55.349 --> 00:19:57.309
All my work is under his cyberlock and key.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.769
Well, can't you just work some of your virtual voodoo and get him back?

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.970
Short of a direct hit from a massive virus.

00:20:05.829 --> 00:20:09.109
All of these files will forever be in the clutches of Citizen Lex.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.230
Maybe I can give him something else to focus on.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:23.900
Cool, huh?

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:25.900
Actually, yeah.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.900
Uh, come here.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:32.900
You don't want Lex or anyone else seeing that you can do that.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.900
Come on, Chloe.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.900
Don't tell me that Clark's got you running scared because of his secret too.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.900
Okay, I know you don't mean that, because this isn't about Clark.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:40.900
Isn't it?

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:44.900
I mean, I remember what it was like covering for him.

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:48.900
Always having to watch what you had to say, lying to you.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.900
To you?

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.299
Oh, so.

00:20:53.299 --> 00:20:55.299
Sometimes you don't have another choice.

00:20:55.299 --> 00:20:56.299
Yes, you do.

00:20:56.299 --> 00:21:00.299
And for once, I'm glad not to be following in Clark's footsteps.

00:21:00.299 --> 00:21:02.299
No secrets, Chloe.

00:21:02.299 --> 00:21:05.299
Putting it on the front page.

00:21:05.299 --> 00:21:08.299
Okay, Pete, I get the whole reach for the stars mentality.

00:21:08.299 --> 00:21:12.299
And right now, you actually could reach a few of those stars.

00:21:12.299 --> 00:21:14.299
But what about all the meteor infective people

00:21:14.299 --> 00:21:16.299
who still appreciate their privacy?

00:21:16.299 --> 00:21:18.299
They want to keep living alive.

00:21:18.299 --> 00:21:28.079
That's their problem.

00:21:28.079 --> 00:21:31.059
Maybe it's time for everyone to realize that a real hero doesn't hide in the

00:21:31.079 --> 00:21:33.079
shadows. Excuse me.

00:21:33.079 --> 00:21:59.660
Are you looking for something?

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.660
Um, Lana.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.660
Um, yeah, I was just...

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:08.660
Kara, I don't think that Clark would appreciate you going through his things.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:24.009
What do you know about these symbols?

00:22:24.009 --> 00:22:26.009
As much as anyone in Smallville, I guess.

00:22:26.009 --> 00:22:28.009
They're from a local Indian tribe.

00:22:28.009 --> 00:22:30.009
Then why were they on the bracelet I used to wear?

00:22:30.009 --> 00:22:34.539
Well, maybe you bought it while you were here visiting the kents,

00:22:34.539 --> 00:22:37.539
or maybe they sent it to you as a present.

00:22:37.539 --> 00:22:43.309
You know, it's amazing.

00:22:43.309 --> 00:22:47.309
How you and Clark can just lie on autopilot like that?

00:22:47.309 --> 00:22:48.309
Kara.

00:22:48.309 --> 00:22:51.309
I know about the symbols burned into the barn.

00:22:51.309 --> 00:22:55.519
And the fields.

00:22:55.519 --> 00:22:56.519
But I know about this.

00:22:56.519 --> 00:23:05.089
A tattoo you somehow don't have anymore.

00:23:05.089 --> 00:23:08.779
Where did you get these?

00:23:08.779 --> 00:23:19.450
Lex.

